; CanonSim Workbench — the semantic-token theme (wb-2, frontend §10–§16;
; wb-10 the first visual pass; wb-12 the token-audit re-pin; iter-232 the
; OLED re-pin — the owner's 2026-09-25 «цвет лучше взять темный под oled
; мониторы, но не синий такой убогий» call, per docs/VISUAL_SYSTEM_UI.md
; the law owner).
;
; The single source of the Workbench visual language (frontend §10: the
; ladder `primitives -> semantic tokens -> component tokens -> component
; states -> composition` — values never scattered into code). Three layers
; live here:
;   1. `Workbench/*` — the semantic TOKEN namespace: colours, type sizes,
;      spacings and the chrome styleboxes. The shell script reads them by
;      name (theme.get_color / get_constant / get_stylebox) — composition
;      code carries token NAMES only, never raw values.
;   2. The component tokens — the styled Control types (Button, the
;      NavButton variation, LineEdit, Label, PanelContainer) with their
;      state sets (default/hover/pressed/hover_pressed/focus/disabled/
;      readonly — §10's component-state law).
;   3. Layered dark surfaces over a TRULY neutral near-black ramp (the
;      iter-232 OLED form below) with WCAG-baseline contrast — the
;      measured pairs noted below.
;
; The iter-232 OLED re-pin (VISUAL_SYSTEM_UI §3's color law, the owner's
; explicit call over the external brief's "never pure black" doctrine —
; AGENTS §2.6: the owner's request in the active session IS the task):
;   - The neutral ramp is TRULY neutral now (R=G=B — the Catppuccin
;     navy-blue tint RETIRED: the owner's «не синий такой убогий»), and
;     the base sits at #050505 — near-pure-black, OLED-friendly (each
;     sub-pixel ~2% duty; the layering survives as pure luminance steps,
;     iter-230's transplanted mechanism unchanged).
;   - ONE accent, TEAL #4cc9a6 (the owner's two named rejections: the
;     iter-230 blue #89b4fa AND the older warm-orange family — teal is
;     the family that is neither); the accent marks interactive
;     affordances and the live/GENERATING state, never decoration.
;   - Role names, token names, sizes, spacings, margins, radii and the
;     NavButton/chip_busy set: UNCHANGED from theme@0.3 (the shell reads
;     by name — this re-pin is values-only, zero shell.gd reads touched
;     beyond the version string).
;
; Contrast pairs (WCAG 2.2 baseline, §12 — measured over the sRGB math,
; scripts/contrast_check.py iter-232):
;   text_primary   #ededed on surface_l2 #131313  15.9:1
;   text_secondary #b9b9b9 on surface_l2            9.5:1
;   text_muted     #8b8b8b on surface_l1 #0b0b0b   5.8:1
;   accent         #4cc9a6 on surface_l2            9.0:1
;   on_accent      #04110c on accent    #4cc9a6    9.4:1
;   border_field   #616161 vs input bg #080808     3.2:1 (non-text, >=3:1)
; Colour is never the sole state channel (§12): states pair with text or
; position. This file is the wb-2 deliverable "the semantic-token theme
; file" (TASKS wb-2, CONTRACTS §5); identity = its sha256 (carried by the
; shell proof metadata).
;
; Theme id: canon_workbench_theme@0.4 (dark OLED — the only admitted theme).

[gd_resource type="Theme" load_steps=22 format=3]

